  "edit_instruction": "Repair the existing derived feature tree to preserve the accepted Harness contracts already in docs/requirements.md. Do not expand product scope or change any canonical source or expected case. Modify only existing feature descriptions/metadata; retain all supported behavior and feature identities. These are corrections of proven drift, not new requirements.\n1. Five-field input is IPv4 TCP/UDP with BOTH source_port and destination_port REQUIRED integer 0..65535; no optional/None flow ports.\n2. Rules have source/destination IPv4 host or canonical CIDR, protocol tcp/udp/any, and BOTH source_ports and destination_ports as REQUIRED inclusive [lower,upper] integer ranges. Match is conjunction of CIDR membership, protocol equal or any, and inclusive membership in both ranges. Do not model rule ports as optional scalar equality. No placeholder predicate semantics or future-schema deferral: this contract is already decided. Action never filters matches; show all permit and deny matches in snapshot order.\n3. Exact input v1 has version, flow, relevance list of device/acl pairs, and snapshots list of device/acl/placements/rules. Placements are owned by snapshots, not relevance records. Synthetic relevance returns input pairs for the provided source/destination; do not invent a relevance_records address-indexed input schema.\n4. Exact JSON report is {version:1,groups:[{device,acl,placements,status:MATCHES|NO_MATCH,rules:[original rule objects]}]}. Preserve original fields and snapshot placements. Do not expose matches, device_id, acl_id or MATCH as public JSON keys/status. Internal types must be able to realize inclusive ranges and preserve original input facts without semantic invention.\n5. Public invocation is python3 -m checker --input PATH [--format text|json]. --input is required. No default stdin. Expected failures exit 2, empty stdout and stderr Checker error: message. There must be a runnable checker module entrypoint. Use repository/package name checker rather than acl_checker or acl-checker; do not invent a different public invocation.\n6. Keep pure matches and application check(flow,relevance,snapshot) with consumer-owned narrow source callables and outer validation/composition; no domain imports of input/filesystem/CLI adapters. No runtime model, network, web, database, global caches, service wrappers or production-device access. Existing independent expected cases remain unchanged.\nMake these constraints explicit in the affected feature descriptions so subsequent skeleton, data-flow and interface planning preserve them. Do not turn verification procedures into additional product features. Retain scope as a small synthetic CLI.\n",
